 body's answer at a block start while tracing (queue 219t): f.PC is the block start, the whole"] [46 1 "// value stack in f.Stack; guardedStep runs the frame on the loop from there."] [53 1 "// AotTracing is whether frames must run on the loop (a trace function or a line tool set): the compiled code's check"] [54 1 "// at each block start and after each direct call."] [67 1 "// setTrace is _PyEval_SetTrace for t: fn None removes it."] [77 19 "// the previous function let go: its __del__ now when that was its last reference (finAddr)"] [81 1 "// traceCall is trace_trampoline: the 'call' event to the thread's trace function, the others to f's f_trace; a result"] [82 1 "// other than None becomes f_trace; an error removes the trace function and f_trace and is returned."] [121 1 "// traceEvent is the legacy tracer's callback for the frame events (monFire's native)."] [145 1 "// monRaise is RAISE at f (runFrames, where the frame's traceback entry is added: CPython's monitor_raise at its error"] [146 1 "// label, not at a re-raise); a callback's error replaces the exception."] [157 1 "// genWrapped is whether c's view ends with the handler codegen wraps a generator's or coroutine's body in"] [158 1 "// (CALL_INTRINSIC_1 INTRINSIC_STOPITERATION_ERROR, RERAISE 1; queue 281): an exception leaving the frame is handled there"] [159 1 "// and raised again (EXCEPTION_HANDLED, RERAISE)."] [169 1 "// monExc is an exception event ev (RERAISE, EXCEPTION_HANDLED) at f; a callback's error replaces the exception."] [180 1 "// monStopIteration is STOP_ITERATION at f (monitor_stop_iteration): a generator or coroutine a yield-from ran to its end"] [181 1 "// with value v, a StopIteration(v) made for the event; RAISE (gen false) for the StopIteration a non-generator delegate"] [182 1 "// raised or a generator's next set for a value other than None (gen_iternext)."] [191 2 "// PyErr_SetObject(PyExc_StopIteration, value): no argument for None"] [199 1 "// traceLines are c's instructions that may start a line event (initialize_lines): a line different from the previous"] [200 1 "// instruction's in code order, a jump's target but a for-iter's, a handler's target; never the RESUME nop at 0."] [218 2 "// FOR_ITER's target is not marked: CPython's is the POP_ITER after its END_FOR, which never starts a line (queue 248)"] [236 1 "// resumeAt0 is whether c starts with its RESUME, the nop arbace.python.compile puts at co_firstlineno (a module has none)."] [241 1 "// inCImpl is whether f runs the Python code that stands for CPython's C (pylifecycle.go's cImplModules: io's _pyio,"] [242 1 "// warnings' _py_warnings; queue 293): no sys.monitoring event fires in its frames, and so no trace or profile event,"] [243 1 "// as none fires inside CPython's C (test_bdb's test_skip: the source loader's open_code is _pyio's open, a Python"] [244 1 "// function, whose 'call' bdb would see). The answer is kept in the code object, from the globals of its first frame."] [252 1 "// standsForC is whether c is of the code that stands for C, its module's globals g (kept in c from its first answer)."] [265 1 "// traceInstr is the loop's hook before f runs instruction f.PC while tracing: the line event (a line's instrumented"] [266 1 "// instruction reached from another line, or after a RESUME: the frame's start, a resumption after a yield), the opcode"] [267 1 "// event, a backward jump's line event. A trace function's jump (f_lineno) changes f.PC: the target then runs with no"] [268 1 "// event of its own. An error is raised at the instruction."] [286 3 "// JUMP, BRANCH_LEFT and BRANCH_RIGHT of the instruction that led here (queue 281)"] [316 3 "// INSTRUCTION: the view's instructions this one came from (a branch's NOT_TAKEN and a loop's POP_ITER are"] [317 3 "// monFlow's, as the path decides them; the view's RESUME fires none)"] [321 5 "// the view's instructions of no IR instruction just before this one's (PUSH_NULL ...), reached in sequence"] [322 5 "// from prev's"] [368 1 "// monFlowFrame and monFlowPC are the frame a JUMP or BRANCH callback runs for and the destination its stack is"] [369 1 "// (f_lineno's setter; under the GIL, no event fires inside a callback)."] [375 1 "// monFlowFire fires a JUMP or BRANCH event (args: the code, its source and destination offsets) of prev to pc: f_lasti"] [376 1 "// the jump while the callbacks run (INSTRUMENTED_JUMP's frame), a callback's f_lineno jump kept (f.PC moved)."] [389 1 "// monFlow is the JUMP or BRANCH event of IR instruction prev, a jump, that led to pc (queue 281): CPython's"] [390 1 "// INSTRUMENTED_JUMP_FORWARD/BACKWARD (JUMP), INSTRUMENTED_POP_JUMP_IF_* (BRANCH_RIGHT, taken), INSTRUMENTED_NOT_TAKEN"] [391 1 "// (BRANCH_LEFT, from the jump past the NOT_TAKEN), INSTRUMENTED_FOR_ITER (BRANCH_LEFT, a next value) and"] [392 1 "// INSTRUMENTED_POP_ITER (BRANCH_RIGHT, the loop's end, past the POP_ITER), their offsets the view's (bytecode_asm.go) for"] [393 1 "// the view's instruction the IR's came from. An IR jump the view has no jump for fires nothing."] [400 3 "// an async for's step: the awaited __anext__'s END_SEND then NOT_TAKEN (BRANCH_LEFT from the END_SEND), its"] [401 3 "// StopAsyncIteration's END_ASYNC_FOR (BRANCH_RIGHT from the END_SEND past it)"] [497 4 "// past the END_FOR the exhausted FOR_ITER skips, the POP_ITER fires the event"] [520 1 "// f_lineno's jumps: the kinds of mark_stacks' slots, three bits each in an int64 (the top the low bits)"] [566 1 "// irEffect is instruction in's stack effect falling through and jumping (arbace.python.ir's table)."] [623 1 "// markStacks is mark_stacks over c's IR: each instruction's stack as its slots' kinds, stackUninit where unreached."] [742 1 "// frameSetLineno is frame_lineno_set_impl: a jump to line v from a trace function's event."] [771 2 "// marklines: each line's first instruction in code order"] [794 29 "// a JUMP or BRANCH callback's: f_lasti the jump, the stack its destination's"] [844 24 "// the value the yield popped"